I. Running Denali Memory Model based Simulation with Modelsim Verilog
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
     In the local "modelsim.ini" file set the following variable in the [vsim]
   section.

     Veriuser = $DENALI/mtipli.so 
     [Please refer to the "modelsim.ini" file in the "Mpmc_rtl" directory.]

   To run the simulation using modelsim, type
   "make TBENCH=<tbench_number> rtl"

   Eg.:
      1.To run the modelsim simulation using tbench7 type
        make TBENCH=7 rtl

      2.To run the modelsim simulation using tbench type
         make TBENCH= rtl

     This command will start the RTL simulations for the Denali tests.


II. Running Denali Memory Model based Simulation with LDV Verilog-XL
    ----------------------------------------------------------------
      For running Denali Memory model based simulations with LDV Verilog-XL, a
    customised local Verilog-XL executable needs to be created. This custom
    Verilog-XL executable will contain the required PLI information. Please
    refer to the following readme help file for the creation of the Verilog-XL
    executable : 
      $DENALI/verilog/README.verilog

    Further tips for the creation of the customised Verilog-XL executable :
      Some of the options to be chosen are as follows - 
      o  Standalone
      o  Generate libpli
      o  Dynamically linked PLI
      o  All other entries as specified in the README.verilog

      o  Set the LD_LIBRARY_PATH environment variable to include the path where
         the new "Verilog-XL" executable and the "libpli.o" files reside.

    Use the new custom created "Verilog-XL" executable for the simulations. 
 
    NOTE : The verification/verilog/tbench/SimMakefile_LDV.mk file needs
           to have the exact name & path of the "Verilog-XL" executable file.
    
   To run the simulation using LDV, type
   "make TBENCH=<tbench_number> rtl"

   Eg.:
      1.To run the LDV simulation using tbench7 type
        make TBENCH=7 rtl

      2.To run the LDV simulation using tbench type
         make TBENCH= rtl

     This command will start the RTL simulations for the Denali tests.

